# OS-level CVEs pending upstream fix in base image
CVE-2026-4878
CVE-2026-29111

# GDAL 3.10.3 (Debian trixie's apt-provided version — no newer version is
# available in the base image's repo; the fix (3.13.1) would require
# building GDAL from source or switching base images entirely). Stack
# buffer overflow in the netCDF driver's scanForGeometryContainers
# (frmts/netcdf/netcdfsg.cpp), triggered only by parsing a crafted .nc
# file. This app never reads NetCDF and never opens arbitrary/untrusted
# files through GDAL — the only usage (app/services/export_service.py) is
# writing outbound Shapefile exports via the ESRI Shapefile OGR driver,
# and app/cli/import_footprints.py reads operator-supplied Shapefile/
# GeoJSON footprint data, not network-facing input. Revisit when Debian
# trixie or a backport channel ships a fixed gdal-bin package.
CVE-2026-49014
